course: dictionary
lesson: 13072
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The noun fertility is about how well something can produce. Its adjective is fertile, so fertile land is land where plants grow well.
explain: «The fertility of the soil near the River Nile helped farmers grow wheat for thousands of years.» The clues are soil, farmers and wheat, so fertility must mean how well the land can grow crops.
explain: «Her fertility of mind meant she always had a new idea for her story.» Here the clue is new ideas, so fertility of mind means being full of ideas. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Fertility is a noun, and its adjective is fertile.
fact: Fertility can mean how well soil or land can grow plants and crops.
fact: Fertility can also mean a living thing's ability to have babies or young.
fact: Fertility of mind means being full of ideas.
fact: Ancient people made statues of fertility goddesses to pray for good harvests and healthy families.
exercise: «Farmers test the soil to check its fertility before they plant crops.» What does fertility mean here? | How many stones are in the soil | How heavy the soil is | The colour of the soil | *How well the soil can grow plants and crops
exercise: Mina says her friend has great fertility of mind. What does she mean? | Her friend has very big feet | Her friend is always tired | Her friend is good at maths only | *Her friend is full of new ideas
exercise: Which word is the adjective of fertility? | fertilizer | fertilise | ferment | *fertile
test: The river flooded and left rich mud, so the fertility of the land went up. What did the flood do to the fertility of the land? | It made the land colder | It removed all the soil | *It helped the land grow more crops | It made the land go to sleep
test: Rabbits have a high fertility, so one pair can have many young. What does fertility mean here? | Living in a hole | *The ability to have babies or young | Being very quiet | Being tall
exam: Which sentence uses fertility correctly? | The fertility sang a song at the party | The fertility of the box was very heavy | *The fertility of the soil helped the farm grow wheat | Fertility is a loud, noisy kind of bird
